# Vivado drops these wherever it's invoked from, regardless of project
# directory -- catch them repo-wide rather than per-subdirectory.
.Xil/
retry_open_fs.log
webtalk*
*.jou
vivado*.log
vivado*.str

# Per-machine tool locations (see hardware/qmtech-kintex7/openxc7/toolchain.sh)
toolchain.local

# WiFi credentials for the CM4 miner -- keep the PSK out of the repo.
# Ships as a template; fill it in locally or on the running board.
hardware/qmtech-kintex7/linux/overlay/etc/wpa_supplicant/wpa_supplicant-wlan0.conf
hardware/qmtech-kintex7/openxc7/gen/

# Stray tool output dropped in the REPO ROOT by scripts invoked from here,
# rather than from the directory that owns them. Named specifically rather
# than as a blanket *.log, so a log someone deliberately commits still shows up.
n_*.log
build_*.log

# openXC7 build artefacts. All regenerable from the committed scripts, and all
# large: out_*/ holds netlists (60-90 MB each), FASMs (63 MB) and bitstreams
# (11 MB); seedrun/ holds a route log per seed.
#
# Ignored primarily to keep `git status` legible. With ~70 untracked artefacts
# in the way, a genuinely modified tracked file does not stand out -- a broken
# hdl/odocrypt/encrypt.v sat in the working tree for a day precisely because it
# was one line among that noise.
hardware/qmtech-kintex7/openxc7/out_*/
hardware/qmtech-kintex7/openxc7/seedrun/
hardware/qmtech-kintex7/openxc7/*.console
hardware/qmtech-kintex7/openxc7/.pid_*
hardware/qmtech-kintex7/openxc7/.done_*

# Vivado diagnostic output from the placement-comparison work. Deliberately NOT
# committed, for a reason the tooling itself states: vivado_place_export_v68.tcl
# documents these maps as "DIAGNOSTIC ONLY -- THIS MAP CANNOT BE COMMITTED AND
# REUSED", because they are keyed on yosys cell names built from volatile
# counters ($abc$493613$..., autoidx). Measured there: two modules differing by
# one unrelated gate shared ZERO cell names. Any RTL edit, yosys upgrade or
# option change invalidates 100% of the map, so a committed copy would be a
# trap rather than an asset.
#
# The durable output of that work is the GEOMETRY, which is encoded in
# floorplan_brams.py --mode compact, and the calibration .tcl scripts, which
# are committed.
hardware/qmtech-kintex7/openxc7/vivado_placement*.txt
hardware/qmtech-kintex7/openxc7/vivado_cellnames.txt
hardware/qmtech-kintex7/openxc7/*.dcp
hardware/qmtech-kintex7/openxc7/vivado_*.console.txt
hardware/qmtech-kintex7/openxc7/vivado_net_delay_calib*.csv

# Regenerable outputs of scripts committed alongside them.
hardware/qmtech-kintex7/openxc7/absorb_report.txt
hardware/qmtech-kintex7/openxc7/tight_setup_hold_pins.txt
hardware/qmtech-kintex7/openxc7/vivado_worst_path_anatomy.txt

# Third-party binaries fetched by post-build.sh (esptool aarch64 tarball).
# Verified by hash at build time; not tracked.
hardware/qmtech-kintex7/linux/dl/
